  "title": "Odd cycles and low oddness",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture If in a bridgeless cubic graph $G$ the cycles of any $2$-factor are odd, then $\\omega(G)\\leq 2$, where $\\omega(G)$ denotes the oddness of the graph $G$, that is, the minimum number of odd cycles in a $2$-factor of $G$.",
